From a071affb5ea72cc7368774e8cfad32e9fb8f6834 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:18:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] compiler: z/OS exceptions, resource strings and
 parameter passing fixes

- s390x: the landing pad receives the exception object in R1 and the
  selector in R2 (XPLINK-64), eh_return_data_regno returns 1 and 2
- llvm/z/OS: landing pads of try..except blocks with typed catch clauses
  get a catch-all clause at the end. The landing pad code re-raises the
  exception if no handler matches, but the phase 1 search of the unwinder
  skips a landing pad whose clauses do not match, so an enclosing handler
  in the same function was never found
- z/OS: the binder does not keep the data parts of the resource string
  table of a unit in order, so the table cannot be walked from START to
  END. Generate a list with the number of entries and pointers to the
  entries per unit (RESSTR_$unit_$$_PTRLIST), which FPC_RESOURCESTRINGTABLES
  points to (used by the RTL with FPC_RESSTR_PTRLIST)
- s390x parameters: records and sets of 1, 2 or 4 bytes are passed as
  integers of the same size (caller and callee disagreed about the position
  of the data in the 64 bit slot on big endian); Pascal records of other
  sizes that do not fill 64 bit slots are passed by reference; passing
  "complex-like" records in floating point registers is disabled for now
  (not supported by the generic code)

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
